{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l2le43hc","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline","year":2011,"examDate":2011,"subject":"physics","chapter":"wave-optics","chapterGroup":"optics","topic":"polarisation","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pa-light-ray-travelling-in-glass-medium-is-incident-on-gla-jee-advanced-physics-units-and-measurements-zhxxzn8kjvjmory0","content":"<p>A light ray travelling in glass medium is incident on glass-air interface at an angle of incidence <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.023ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.061ex\" height=\"1.618ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 469 715\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D703\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D703\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. The reflected (R) and transmitted (T) intensities, both as function of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.023ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.061ex\" height=\"1.618ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 469 715\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D703\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D703\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, are plotted. The correct sketch is</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l2mkk70q/915c3031-d677-490c-ae72-861c7c9eb8b5/b3310ea0-c8e7-11ec-8c2d-13f33da2fbe1/file-1l2mkk70r.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l2mkk70q/915c3031-d677-490c-ae72-861c7c9eb8b5/b3310ea0-c8e7-11ec-8c2d-13